WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:04.650
In this video, we're talking about how to identify multiplication and how to distinguish multiplication

00:04.650 --> 00:06.330
from addition and subtraction.

00:06.330 --> 00:11.030
So the first thing we need to know is that there are three ways that we can indicate multiplication.

00:11.040 --> 00:17.610
The good old time sign this X symbol here times meaning three times two or three multiplied by two,

00:17.610 --> 00:19.200
which we know is six.

00:19.200 --> 00:23.820
We have this dot six times one is going to be equal to six.

00:23.820 --> 00:28.860
This also indicates multiplication or two numbers sitting next to each other, one in parentheses or

00:28.860 --> 00:29.670
two in parentheses.

00:29.670 --> 00:30.420
It doesn't matter.

00:30.420 --> 00:32.250
Both of these indicate multiplication.

00:32.250 --> 00:37.600
So four times five is 20, or three times four is 12.

00:37.620 --> 00:39.990
These are all symbols of multiplication.

00:39.990 --> 00:44.970
The thing to remember is that if you don't have an addition or subtraction sign in between the numbers,

00:44.970 --> 00:46.920
then the operation is multiplication.

00:46.920 --> 00:52.320
So if we take a look at a couple more complex examples here, what we can see is that we have some addition

00:52.320 --> 00:55.530
and subtraction signs and we have some numbers that are multiplied together.

00:55.530 --> 01:00.300
So what you can almost do is put parentheses around the things that are multiplied together, which

01:00.300 --> 01:04.410
is just like separating the expression in between the addition and subtraction signs.

01:04.410 --> 01:08.520
So here we have three minus, we have a subtraction sign and then two times five.

01:08.520 --> 01:10.740
So we know this is going to be multiplication here.

01:10.740 --> 01:14.580
Then we have a subtraction sign and then we have six times a negative two.

01:14.610 --> 01:18.690
This is going to be a multiplication and then we have plus two times five.

01:18.690 --> 01:19.860
The two times five.

01:19.860 --> 01:20.700
That's just like this.

01:20.700 --> 01:21.510
Four times five.

01:21.540 --> 01:22.650
Here, that's multiplication.

01:22.650 --> 01:24.360
So this is going to be multiplication.

01:24.360 --> 01:29.460
And what you can see now is that we've separated the expression, we've indicated the multiplication

01:29.460 --> 01:33.270
with these brackets and everything in between now is an addition or subtraction sign.

01:33.270 --> 01:37.560
So we have a subtraction sign, a subtraction sign, and in addition sign here.

01:37.560 --> 01:42.360
So we want to do our multiplication first according to order of operations will leave our addition and

01:42.360 --> 01:45.330
subtraction signs and then we'll do those operations next.

01:45.330 --> 01:48.570
So we're going to have three minus two times five is ten.

01:48.570 --> 01:50.820
We keep our subtraction sign six times.

01:50.820 --> 01:56.880
A negative two is a -12 and we want to put parentheses around it so that we keep this negative sign

01:56.880 --> 01:59.760
here separate from the subtraction sign that we left in between.

01:59.760 --> 02:02.280
Then we have plus two times five is ten.

02:02.280 --> 02:06.000
Now we can simplify further because we have a minus, a -12.

02:06.000 --> 02:08.070
That's the same thing as saying plus 12.

02:08.070 --> 02:11.370
So this becomes three minus ten plus 12.

02:11.370 --> 02:15.570
In other words, the two negative signs cancel with each other and become a positive.

02:15.570 --> 02:17.730
So plus 12 plus ten.

02:17.730 --> 02:21.990
Now, at this point, we can add all of our positive numbers together and then add all of our negative

02:21.990 --> 02:24.000
numbers together and get our final result.

02:24.000 --> 02:26.250
So here we have a positive three.

02:26.250 --> 02:30.930
Plus a positive 12 is 15 plus a positive ten is 25.

02:30.930 --> 02:33.240
So this is going to become 25.

02:33.390 --> 02:36.210
And then our single negative number is this negative ten.

02:36.210 --> 02:37.590
So we have minus ten.

02:37.590 --> 02:41.160
And that's going to be equal to, of course, just positive 15.

02:41.160 --> 02:42.960
Let's look at our second example here.

02:42.960 --> 02:46.380
We're going to again put brackets around our multiplication.

02:46.380 --> 02:50.580
So we have two times four indicated with the good old time sign here.

02:50.580 --> 02:55.200
So two times four we have minus and then three times two indicated with the dot.

02:55.200 --> 03:00.210
So three times two minus a seven plus five times two.

03:00.210 --> 03:02.310
So again, multiplication here.

03:02.310 --> 03:07.260
Now we've got brackets around our multiplication and we have every sign in between just an addition

03:07.260 --> 03:08.310
or subtraction sign.

03:08.310 --> 03:12.000
So we have, of course, subtraction, subtraction and addition.

03:12.000 --> 03:17.250
Now if we do our multiplication first, leaving our addition and subtraction in between two times four

03:17.250 --> 03:18.120
gives us eight.

03:18.150 --> 03:24.060
We keep our subtraction sign three times, two gives us six, keep our subtraction seven, keep our

03:24.060 --> 03:27.150
addition, and then five times two is ten.

03:27.150 --> 03:31.410
Now we can do the same thing we did before we add up all of our positive numbers and then add up all

03:31.410 --> 03:36.450
of our negative numbers, or we can just do the addition and subtraction together, moving left to right.

03:36.450 --> 03:38.400
So eight minus six is two.

03:38.430 --> 03:40.650
Two minus seven is a negative five.

03:40.650 --> 03:43.140
Negative five plus ten is a positive five.

03:43.140 --> 03:45.600
So our final answer is positive five.
